    "### 2. Define Release Sources\n",
    "\n",
    "Each source is a dictionary with a `name`, a `location`, and a `schedule`. Add\n",
    "or remove entries here to release from as many places as you like. Nothing in\n",
    "this cell touches the grid yet, so it is safe to edit freely.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Location types**\n",
    "- `\"line\"` — a straight release line. Give either `row` (fixed) + `cols=(c0, c1)`,\n",
    "  or `col` (fixed) + `rows=(r0, r1)`. Ranges are inclusive.\n",
    "- `\"point\"` — a single cell `row, col`, optionally repeated `n_cells` times.\n",
    "- `\"points\"` — an explicit list of `(row, col)` cells under `cells`.\n",
    "- `\"mask\"` — every cell where a 2-D array is truthy. Pass `mask=<2D bool array>`,\n",
    "  or `grid=<2D array>` together with `equals=<value>`.\n",
    "- `\"latlon\"` — geographic release point(s). Pass `lat` and `lon` (scalars or\n",
    "  lists); they are projected with `utm_proj` and converted with `pt.coord2ind`.\n",
    "  Give matching lists to trace a line release.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Schedule types**\n",
    "- `\"particles_csv\"` — a ready-made CSV of particles per day (`date_col`, `value_col`).\n",
    "- `\"discharge_csv\"` — a discharge CSV converted to particles per day\n",
    "  (`date_col`, `q_col`, optional `smooth_days`, `scale`, `positive_only`).\n",
    "- `\"constant\"` — a flat `rate_per_day` between `start` and `end`. **Use this for a\n",
    "  tributary whose discharge you do not know yet**; set a nominal rate now and swap\n",
    "  in a real CSV later without changing anything else.\n",
    "- `\"series\"` — inline `dates` and `counts` lists."
   ]
  },
